---
title: Braised Tofu with Shiitake (Dong Gu Mun Tofu 冬菇豆腐)
description: Earthy and savory braised tofu with fresh shiitake mushrooms in a glossy oyster sauce gravy.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - tofu
  - vegetarian
  - chinese
  - mushroom
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/braised-tofu-shiitake
cuisine: Chinese
course: Main
---

== Fry the Tofu ==
Heat @neutral oil{14%g} in a #pan{}. Fry the @extra-firm tofu{350%g} (cubed) until golden on a few sides. Remove and set aside.

== Sauté Aromatics and Mushrooms ==
-- Sautéing ginger and scallions releases their essential oils
Add a little more oil to the pan if needed. Sauté the @ginger{2%slices}, @scallions{1%sliced}, and @fresh shiitake mushrooms{250%g} (halved) for ~{2%minutes} until the mushrooms begin to soften.

== Braise ==
Mix the sauce: combine @chicken broth{250%g}, @oyster sauce{35%g}, @light soy sauce{15%g}, and @sugar{4%g}.
Pour the sauce mixture into the pan and return the tofu. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat, cover, and simmer gently for ~{15%minutes}.

== Thicken ==
-- The slurry gives the sauce a glossy, clinging texture
Mix the slurry: @cornstarch{8%g} and @cold water{15%g}.
Stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook for ~{1%minute} until the sauce becomes glossy and clings to the tofu.
